Here is a simple Shadertoy shader for a rotating square:
```scss
// Create a new shader
Shader "Custom/Rotating Square" {
    Tags {"Queue"="Transparent" "RenderType"="Transparent"}
    LOD 200

    // Set the square's position and rotation
    Property {
        Tag "Object"
        Key "Position" {
            Vector {0, 0, 0, 0}
        }
        Key "Rotation" {
            Float 0
        }
    }

    SubShader {
        Tags {"RenderType"="Transparent"}
        LOD 200

        // Set the square's color
        CGPROGRAM
        #pragma surface surf Lambert

        sampler2D _MainTex;
        struct Input {
            float2 uv_MainTex;
        };

        void surf (Input IN, inout SurfaceOutput o) {
            // Set the square's color based on its position and rotation
            o.Albedo = tex2D(_MainTex, IN.uv_MainTex).rgb;
            o.Alpha = tex2D(_MainTex, IN.uv_MainTex).a;
        }
        ENDCG
    }
    FallBack "Diffuse"
}
```
To use this shader, create a new material and select the "Custom/Rotating Square" shader from the shader list. Then, in your scene, create a new game object and assign the material to it. You can then adjust the square's position and rotation in the inspector to see it rotate in real-time.

